## Django URLs Guidelines

### URL Patterns

- Use Django's URL dispatcher (urls.py) to define clear and RESTful URL patterns
- Implement proper URL namespacing for different apps
- Use descriptive URL patterns that reflect the resource
- Implement versioned API URLs when needed

### API URLs

- Structure API URLs following REST conventions
- Use DRF router for ViewSet URLs
- Implement proper URL patterns for CRUD operations
- Use nested URLs for related resources

### WebSocket Routing

- Configure WebSocket routing in routing.py files
- Implement proper URL patterns for WebSocket consumers
- Handle WebSocket connection URLs
- Structure routing for different WebSocket applications

### URL Configuration

- Use include() for app-specific URLs
- Implement proper URL parameter handling
- Use path() and re_path() appropriately
- Handle URL redirects and reverse lookups

### Security

- Validate URL parameters
- Implement proper URL access controls
- Use HTTPS URLs in production
- Handle URL-based attacks (path traversal, etc.)
